ons to internal peer hosts not seen in typical communication baselines, used to proxy or forward traffic internally, often using SMB, RPC, or high ports.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0204","platforms":["Windows"],"tuning":[{"field":"InternalConnectionPattern","description":"Tune based on known host-to-host communications that are rare (e.g., workstation-to-workstation)."},{"field":"DestinationPort","description":"Focus on unusual internal traffic on ports like 1080, 8080, 4444, or SMB over non-standard ports."},{"field":"TimeWindow","description":"Correlate unusual traffic bursts with new process execution."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0204","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0204","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0204","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0204","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"Windows Firewall Log","channel":"SMB over high port","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0204","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0204","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"}]},{"id":"AN0205","name":"Analytic 0205","guidance":"`socat`, `ssh`, `iptables`, or `ncat` invoked from user space or cron jobs to create port forwarding, reverse shells, or inter-host tunnels between compromised Linux systems. Behavior is typically paired with socket activity and high entropy traffic.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0205","platforms":["Linux"],"tuning":[{"field":"UserContext","description":"Alert on unexpected users executing inter-host relay tools (e.g., `www-data`, `backup`)."},{"field":"PortRange","description":"Adjust to watch for commonly misused internal TCP/UDP ports."},{"field":"ProcessPattern","description":"Shell pipelines or wrapped invocations like `bash -c 'socat ...'`"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"auditd:SYSCALL","channel":"execve","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0205","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0205","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"NSM:Connections","channel":"Internal connection logging","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0205","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0205","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"component_id":"DC0085","component":"Network Traffic Content","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"conn.log","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0205","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0205","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}]},{"id":"AN0206","name":"Analytic 0206","guidance":"Execution of AppleScript or Automator services launching `ssh -L`, `socat`, or `launchctl` items that dynamically reroute traffic from one Mac endpoint to another. LaunchAgents used to establish permanent internal tunnels.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0206","platforms":["macOS"],"tuning":[{"field":"LaunchAgentPath","description":"Directory where proxying LaunchDaemons may be dropped, e.g., `/Library/LaunchDaemons/`."},{"field":"PortBindings","description":"Dynamic port forwards often use ephemeral or non-standard service ports."},{"field":"AppleScriptUsage","description":"May trigger on less common scripting interfaces for traffic redirection."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"macos:unifiedlog","channel":"None","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0206","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0206","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0078","component":"Network Traffic Flow","name":"NSM:Flow","channel":"pf firewall logs","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0206","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0206","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"component_id":"DC0060","component":"Service Creation","name":"macos:osquery","channel":"Process Events and Launch Daemons","platforms":["macOS"],"analytic_id":"AN0206","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0206","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0060/"}]},{"id":"AN0207","name":"Analytic 0207","guidance":"ESXi shell execution of tools/scripts (`nc`, `socat`, `perl`) relaying network traffic to other internal hosts, especially when initiated by unauthorized users or VMs.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0075#AN0207","platforms":["ESXi"],"tuning":[{"field":"CLICommandPattern","description":"Watch for chained shell commands building local-to-local connections."},{"field":"VMInitiator","description":"Correlate to which VM initiated the traffic tunnel; unexpected VM behavior may be suspicious."},{"field":"ConnectionDirectionality","description":"Unusual east-west communication patterns among VMs."}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"esxi:shell","channel":"/var/log/shell.log","platforms":["ESXi"],"analytic_id":"AN0207","source_url":"https://attack